 "transcriber_notes": "Measured on the embedded 6160x2832 chart raster (the PDF page crops it to the left half). Boundaries printed on the right axis and confirmed by bar/boundary lines in the plot (+-0.2 cm). Hardness from bar left edges against the grey gridlines (I/K/P/1F/4F/F at 707/967/1227/1487/1747/2007 px, 260 px per class; one third of a class read as +/-). Bar ends: 2010=F, 1920=F+, 1490=1F, 1400=1F+, 1140=P+, 1836=4F-, 1230=P. TEMPERATURE AXIS IS IN DEG F (-16..32 F, labels only, no tick marks). Temperatures are vertices of a continuous red polyline without markers, converted with the Avanet template geometry (32 F = 0 C at x=2115.5 px, 46.80 px/C); every vertex falls on a whole degree C (+-0.02 C), the 122 cm corner located by intersecting the fitted segments; no printed air temperature to cross-check. Treating F-label left edges as ticks would give values ~0.37 C warmer. Line runs from the surface to 50 cm (no values below). Water content column empty for every row. Avanet two-linked-circle glyph mapped to MFcr; dome-on-box glyph mapped to FCxr."
